  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere rolls without slipping along the track shown in the figure. The sphere starts from rest from a height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> above the bottom of the loop of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> which is much larger than the radius of the sphere <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>. The minimum value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> for the sphere to complete the loop is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-08-12_at_3.36.27_PM.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 114px;\" />",
